      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also ran into this (or a very similar) issue today playing on the Android app to test quest and Android upload compatibility and features. My partner's character upload is 'quest poor', and if I understand it correctly, 'poor' rating should still be visible on the Android app, but only the imposter was displayed for me with no option for me as the viewer to show or choose to display the avatar. \n\n His private upload avatar id is avtr_3eb78dd8-d9d7-4529-aa15-414cdbdfd5c6\n\nQuest Poor due to: 19366 polygons, 8 phys bone components, 36 phys bone transforms. Everything else is medium to excellent. Including texture memory at excellent 6.575986 mb\n\nThe reason I'm the one reporting it is that i am unable to view him on the Android app, but he can view himself. Im also the one who creates and maintains the unity projects for our household. So I'm the one who optimized his character trying to be within the 'poor' quest limit and i would like to get it compatible in a reliable, repeatable, known limits kind of way. \n\nBut if the known limit is not 'quest poor' .. what is it? \n\nI don't know what's up unless this is a bug of some kind. We do not own quest headsets to test quest content, so the Android app is the only way for us.",
